# 🤝 17. Behavioral Question

## Question

**How do you troubleshoot a technical problem?**

### Answer

> I start by gathering information and understanding the exact symptoms. I ask questions about when the issue started, what changed, and whether other users are affected. I then identify possible causes and begin with basic troubleshooting steps. I use evidence such as error messages, system information, and logs rather than making assumptions. After making an appropriate change, I verify the result with the user, document the resolution, and escalate the issue if it requires additional access or expertise.

