# 🧠 18. Technical Wording Improvements

Today's practice also focused on using professional IT terminology.

Instead of:

> "Power on self test when computer starts."

Use:

> **"POST is a startup diagnostic process that checks essential hardware before the operating system loads."**

Instead of:

> "Check the power device."

Use:

> **"Check the power source, outlet, power strip, and power cable."**

Instead of:

> "Check the display cable."

Use:

> **"Check the video cable and confirm it is connected to the correct display output."**

Instead of:

> "Check if the OS file is showing."

Use:

> **"Check whether the storage device is detected and whether the system has a valid bootable operating system."**

Instead of:

> "RAM erases everything."

Use:

> **"RAM is volatile memory, so its contents are lost when power is removed."**

Instead of:

> "How computer is boot."

Use:

> **"Boot order determines the sequence of devices the computer checks for a bootable operating system."**

